Run cat > /tmp/pr712-review.json <<'EOF'
{
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Review Summary\n\n**Task:** @01KK6BECKPA5MHQAZJ2KNPEMP1\n**Spec:** @config-shadow\n\n### Own AC Coverage\n- [x] ac-11 has direct behavioral coverage in `tests/shadow.test.ts` for pull-before-push and pre-read sync paths\n- [ ] ac-12 is not covered against the production scheduler implementation; the new test file copies the class instead of importing the shipped code\n\n### Trait AC Coverage\n- Targeted review only. I checked the new/changed user-facing error paths, but repo-wide `kspec validate` is currently noisy for unrelated meta issues.\n\n### Code Quality\n- MUST-FIX: `tests/shadow-sync-scheduler.test.ts` mirrors `ShadowSyncScheduler` instead of importing it, so the test suite can pass while the production daemon scheduler regresses.\n- MUST-FIX: the new pre-read sync path in `initContext()` drops configured shadow branch/remote options, so custom `shadow.branch` / `shadow.remote` setups silently skip sync or consult the wrong tracking config.\n- MUST-FIX: the new remote-branch existence checks in shadow pull/push logic still default to `origin`, which breaks the bidirectional sync behavior for the non-`origin` remotes that `@config-shadow` already supports.\n\n### Regression Check\n- `npm test` is red on the current PR head (`tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts`, 11 failures). Those failures look outside this diff, but the full regression gate is not clean right now.\n\n### Quality Gates\n- [x] Spec intent reviewed\n- [ ] Own AC coverage complete on shipped code\n- [ ] Configured-remote behavior preserved\n- [ ] Full regression suite clean on current head",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "tests/shadow-sync-scheduler.test.ts",
      "line": 15,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This file copies `ShadowSyncScheduler` instead of importing the production class, so `@config-shadow ac-12` is not actually covered on the shipped daemon code path. A regression in `packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts` could pass this suite unchanged."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/parser/yaml.ts",
      "line": 393,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This pre-read sync path drops the resolved shadow config. `hasRemoteTracking(specDir)` and `shadowPull(specDir)` fall back to `kspec-meta`/`origin`, so custom `shadow.branch` or `shadow.remote` setups silently skip sync or use the wrong upstream. Pass the resolved shadow options through here."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/parser/shadow.ts",
      "line": 1330,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: `remoteBranchExists(projectRoot, branchName)` still defaults to `origin`. That breaks the new bidirectional sync flow for configured remotes (`shadow.remote` named/path/url), which is already part of `@config-shadow`. This remote lookup needs to follow the branch's configured upstream, not hardcode the default."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/parser/shadow.ts",
      "line": 1571,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: same issue in the pull path: `fetchRemote(projectRoot)` and the subsequent `remoteBranchExists(...)` probe `origin` instead of the configured shadow remote. That means CLI pre-read sync and daemon pulls are still wrong for non-`origin` shadow remotes."
    }
  ]
}
EOF

